    "solution": "Given: Sum of zeroes (S) = 4, Product of zeroes (P) = 1.\nThe quadratic polynomial is k[x² - Sx + P].\np(x) = k[x² - 4x + 1].\nLet k = 1.\np(x) = x² - 4x + 1.\nSo, one such polynomial is x² - 4x + 1.",
